srv: take the library's read lock before Context.lock

Context.search(), Context.get_categories() and Context.get_tag_browser()
take Context.lock and then call into the library, which takes its read
lock. get_books (srv/code.py) and ajax search (srv/ajax.py) hold the read
lock and then call Context.search(), which takes Context.lock. Two orders
for one pair of locks. Once a writer is queued, SHLock makes new readers
wait behind it, and three threads wait on each other for good:

  - the tag browser holds Context.lock and waits for the read lock;
  - a write waits for the write lock;
  - a page of books holds the read lock and waits for Context.lock.

The tag browser's generate() runs on the server's event-loop thread
(etagged_dynamic_response), so the whole server stops: no request is
served and SIGTERM is ignored. It shows within 15 s at 32 clients with 5%
writes.

This runs all three methods under db.safe_read_lock, taken before
Context.lock, so there is one order everywhere. The read lock is reentrant
for a thread that already holds it, even with a writer queued, so callers
that hold it are unaffected, and safe_read_lock does nothing for a thread
that holds the write lock.

One thing below these methods needs the write lock: Cache.get_categories()
repairs a link table that names a missing item (InvalidLinkTable) by
taking it, and a thread holding the read lock cannot, so SHLock raises
LockingError. read_locked() catches exactly that, runs the repair with no
lock held, and runs the method again. Holding nothing while it waits for
the write lock also fixes a hang the repair has today: it waits for the
write lock while holding Context.lock, so a page of books that holds the
read lock and then searches waits on it for good. A caller that already
holds the read lock, as ajax.py's category handlers do, still gets the
LockingError it gets today.

Separately, and not done here: the tag browser's generate() should not run
on the event-loop thread. Any wait there stalls the whole server.

calibre's srv tests pass (50 run, 2 skipped, 0 failures). Forced-
interleaving tests for the deadlock and for the repair (calibre-zen's
src/calibre_zen/tests/test_srvfix.py, TagBrowserDeadlock and
LinkTableRepair) pass with this change.

